<title>LATVIA: BA CUTS LONDON-RIGA FARE TO $249.</title>
<headline>BA CUTS LONDON-RIGA FARE TO $249.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways on Monday said it was introducing a special offer price of $249 for a return ticket to London for the months of April, May and June.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it was cutting the price by $50 and that one change would be permitted to the reservation which would cost $60.</p>
<p>BA, one of the world's leading airline, started flights between London and Riga at the end of March, becoming the fifth major Western airline to link the Latvian capital.</p>
<p>-- Patrick Lannin, Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
